# The measured library: the tensor4all fork of faer.
#
# The recorder materialises *this* revision in the checkout it is handed and records
# it as `library.commit`, so the pin is what a run measures and what names the page:
# move it before recording, not after.
#
# Revision history: `22f23cf` from repository creation (2026-10-13, the merge of
# tensor4all/faer#7) until the first recording was prepared; `bfe4041` after that,
# which carries tensor4all/faer#13 (the row-split gate for the block Householder
# apply), #14 (the blocked LU's trailing-update floor) and the records from #15 / #17;
# `5578ccc` from 2026-10-18, the merge of the adopted row-major QR/LU work
# (measured at `fe41bbd`, merged at `1d75476`); and now `2240b07`, the merge of the
# two optimizations adopted on 2026-10-18 - `0627828` (the block Householder apply's
# column split takes the whole thread budget) and `2000dd9` (the native gemm thread
# budget is decided in flops). Both were measured at those revisions and the merge
# carries their measured trees (`git diff 2000dd9 2240b07 -- faer/src faer-traits/src
# faer-macros/src Cargo.toml Cargo.lock` is empty), so the measurements were not
# repeated. The fork's own `faer/Cargo.toml` carries package `t4a-faer` 0.24.4.
#
# The four `-timing-v2` pages recorded on 2026-10-15/16 linked the crates.io
# `t4a-faer 0.24.5` and are not evidence about any revision; see
# `docs/reviews/20261016-linked-crate-provenance.md`. Every recording from `5578ccc`
# on linked the checkout (the build script refuses a graph that does not).
# `2870062` from 2026-10-19, the merge of `0c71ca2` (the blocked partial-pivoting
# LU's recursion floor counts work in flops, not elements) on top of `b7715c5`
# (the empty-extent / K0 correctness fix, merged for correctness with no declared
# benchmark path). The floor change was measured as `2870062` against `b7715c5` on
# the `lu`/`solve`/`full_piv_lu`/`cholesky`/`gemm` grid at 1/4/8T, both orders and
# dtypes; the merge is a fast-forward, so the merged tree is the measured tree.
# `a5e6b7d` from 2026-10-19, the merge of the kernel fix: `t4a-private-gemm-x86 0.1.24`
# (256-bit masked-store offset clamped, generated assembly symbols prefixed `t4a_` so the
# campaign's harness can link it next to upstream's `private-gemm-x86`). Recorded as the
# full declared `faer-kernels` suite on both arms - MKL `20261019T025721Z` (15,156 rows,
# full) and OpenBLAS `20261019T052233Z` (20,016 rows, the two-engine arm) - so this is the
# first revision whose pages come from a post-merge periodic run rather than an adoption pair.
# `50c2b98` from 2026-10-19, the merge of the row-major copy floor (`faer#23`), moved
# without re-recording because the only declared cells whose code path changes are
# `linalg-small/32` for lu, full_piv_lu, solve, qr_factor, qr, svd_values and svd_thin:
# the floor is 4096 elements, so 64^2 = 4096 and everything above it take the copy
# exactly as at `a5e6b7d`, and tall/wide are far above it. Those 32-square cells were
# measured as a pair (`20261019T163156Z-base-rm-floor-r2` against
# `20261019T170716Z-cand-rm-floor-4k`, 288 cells at 4T/8T, control 0.9976 with one cell
# outside): 29 faster, 1 slower, and the slower one is a `householder_apply` cell the
# change cannot reach. The published `a5e6b7d` pages therefore understate the 32-square
# cells by 1.4-1.8x on `qr_factor` and are exact everywhere else; the next publication
# replaces them. 1T at 32 was not re-measured: at 1T the copy never paid, and the change
# removes it.
50c2b989484f063f4e1b132adc333715391d8b73
